From: Tim Michals <tcmichals@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH RFC 0/5] remoteproc: sunxi: Add Allwinner XuanTie E907 RemoteProc and Message Box support

This RFC patch series introduces mainline Linux support for the Alibaba
T-Head XuanTie E907 (RV32IMAFCX @ 200 MHz) RISC-V auxiliary co-processor
integrated into Allwinner A523, A527, and T527 (sun55i) SoCs.

The series adds a standalone 4-port hardware Message Box driver, the
XuanTie RemoteProc driver, the associated Devicetree binding schemas,
and DTS node enablement.

Background & Hardware Architecture
==================================
Allwinner sun55i SoCs integrate an octa-core ARM Cortex-A55 cluster
alongside an auxiliary XuanTie E907 RISC-V co-processor. The co-processor
boots from on-chip dedicated SRAM Space 0 (Host PA 0x07280000 / Core DA
0x3FFC0000, 256 KB), can access secondary switchable SRAM Space 1 (Host PA
0x072C0000 / Core DA 0x40000000, 256 KB), and interacts with external DDR
DRAM across the SoC's internal AXI bus.

Inter-processor communication (IPC) is coordinated via a 4-port hardware
Message Box controller (CPUX_MSGBOX at 0x03003000). The mailbox acts as a
star crossbar connecting four processors on the silicon die:
  - Port 0: ARM Cortex-A55 host cluster
  - Port 1: Cadence Tensilica HiFi4 Audio DSP
  - Port 2: Power Management Unit (CPUS)
  - Port 3: XuanTie E907 RISC-V co-processor

The Cortex-A55 exposes 12 logical channels (4 per remote processor),
where Channels 8..11 route directly to the XuanTie E907.

Hardware Validation & Silicon Evidence
======================================
This driver series has been extensively validated on physical silicon using
the Radxa Cubie A5E development board (Allwinner A527 / T527) running
mainline Linux 7.1.0 PREEMPT_RT.

The following automated test suite was executed natively on target hardware
(with full bare-metal firmware test sources available):
  1. testBasic.elf: Core reset de-assertion, SRAM Space 0 boot, MISA CSR
     verification (0x40901125), and heartbeat logging via debugfs trace0.
  2. testStringBinaryTrace0.elf: Sustained trace0 ring-buffer streaming,
     hardware single-precision FPU math (sine wave calculation), and packed
     32-byte binary telemetry parsing.
  3. testCrash.elf: Machine-mode exception trap (mtvec) verification,
     capturing full register autopsy (mepc, mcause=0x2, 31 GPRs) and
     0xDEADF00D signature to SRAM upon intentional illegal instruction,
     while the ARM Linux host kernel remains 100% stable without panicking.
  4. testPingRpmsg.elf: Full Linux VirtIO RPMsg framework validation over
     dynamic DDR CMA buffers (dma_alloc_coherent). Tested 1,000 round-trip
     ping-pong packets with 100% success rate (0 timeouts), averaging
     175.64 us latency and 5.37 MB/s bidirectional bandwidth at 512-byte
     VirtIO buffer size.

PREEMPT_RT Real-Time Compliance
===============================
When the E907 announces a new RPMsg channel via Name Service announcement,
the kernel's rpmsg_char/virtio_rpmsg_bus layers acquire sleeping mutexes
(device_register, blocking_notifier_call_chain). Calling these from
hard-IRQ context triggers "scheduling while atomic" warnings on PREEMPT_RT
kernels. In sunxi_rproc.c, the mailbox callback defers the VirtIO vring
interrupt handler via schedule_work(&priv->vq_work), ensuring 100% clean
operation on PREEMPT_RT kernels.

Design Decisions for Maintainer Review
======================================
1. Standalone drivers/mailbox/sun55i-msgbox.c vs sun6i-msgbox.c:
   The existing sun6i-msgbox.c driver is architected around a legacy
   2-core point-to-point mailbox with flat global registers. The sun55i
   hardware is a 4-processor crossbar where registers are banked per
   processor in independent 0x100-byte apertures with hardware routing
   tables and 8-entry FIFOs. Integrating sun55i into sun6i-msgbox would
   require if-else branching in every function; a clean standalone
   controller driver was implemented instead. Feedback on this design
   choice is welcome.

2. Devicetree YAML Schemas:
   Both allwinner,sun55i-a523-msgbox.yaml and allwinner,sun55i-rproc.yaml
   have been created and pass checkpatch.pl with 0 errors.

